From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: repaint the frame uncovered by a larger caption region

Purpose: paint the whole menu bar after a Luna window grows. The external
shell keeps a rounded caption region sized to the window. When a window
was maximized or widened, the frame was painted while the previous,
smaller region still clipped it; the region was then replaced with
SetWindowRgn(..., FALSE), which does not repaint. The caption was drawn
again afterwards, but the right end of the menu bar stayed black (Wine's
Notepad and the Domino sequencer showed it after maximizing). When the new
region adds visible area, invalidate that non-client part so DefWindowProc
paints it. Limited to the regions managed for the opted-in external shell.
No Microsoft binary is changed.

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/window.c b/dlls/uxtheme/window.c
index 4fda410..1a230f2 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/window.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/window.c
@@ -140,6 +140,24 @@ static void caption_region_update(HWND hwnd, HTHEME theme, const RECT *caption,
         if (region->managed) DeleteObject(region->managed);
         region->managed = copy;
         copy = NULL;
+        /* The previous region clipped any frame painting done before this
+         * resize finished, and SetWindowRgn(..., FALSE) does not repaint.
+         * Repaint the non-client part that the larger region now shows,
+         * such as the right end of a menu bar after maximizing. */
+        if (kind != ERROR && CombineRgn(current, region->managed, current, RGN_DIFF) > NULLREGION)
+        {
+            RECT client;
+            POINT origin = {0, 0};
+            HRGN area = CreateRectRgn(0, 0, 0, 0);
+            GetClientRect(hwnd, &client);
+            ClientToScreen(hwnd, &origin);
+            if (area && CombineRgn(area, current, NULL, RGN_COPY) != ERROR)
+            {
+                OffsetRgn(area, window.left - origin.x, window.top - origin.y);
+                RedrawWindow(hwnd, NULL, area, RDW_INVALIDATE | RDW_FRAME | RDW_NOCHILDREN);
+            }
+            if (area) DeleteObject(area);
+        }
     }
 
 done:
